  "body": "Sanitize while parsing, instead of parsing into a fragment and then walking it.\r\n\r\nThe sanitizer configuration is passed into the HTML parser, which consults it wherever it would create or insert a node: disallowed elements are never created or inserted (or are replaced by their children, by redirecting insertions to where the element would have gone), disallowed attributes are dropped before the element is created, and disallowed comments and processing instructions are discarded. The separate post-parse \"sanitize\" algorithm is gone; the safe variants are expressed by applying their restrictions to the configuration up front.\r\n\r\nConsequences of doing this in the parser:\r\n\r\n- No custom element constructors run for elements the sanitizer discards (they get no definition and a null registry), and no speculative fetches are started while sanitizing.\r\n- When sanitizing, fragment parsing builds its result in the inert document and adopts it into the target afterwards, so discarded elements never exist in the target document (#12560).\r\n- Declarative shadow roots are only attached when `<template>` and `shadowrootmode` survive the configuration; `<template for>` patching as well.\r\n- Insertion locations are computed after element creation, since creating a customized built-in can run script. The adoption agency algorithm and the Noah's Ark clause are adjusted so that removed/replaced elements and stripped attributes don't affect them (the latter now compares token attributes, matching all engines).\r\n\r\nWeb-observable changes compared to the post-parse sanitizer:\r\n\r\n- Adjacent text nodes are coalesced at parse time (e.g. text around a removed or replaced element ends up in one Text node).\r\n- No custom element constructors run for, and no customized built-ins are created from, elements or is attributes that the sanitizer discards.\r\n- For fragment parses: a top-level <template shadowrootmode> no longer attaches a shadow root to the context element, and when sanitizing, elements are created in an inert document before being adopted into the target's document.\r\n\r\nCloses #12560\r\nCloses #12543 \r\n\r\n<!--\r\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\r\n\r\nWhen you submit this PR, and each time you edit this comment (including checking a checkbox through the UI!), PR Preview will run and update it. As such make any edits in one go and only after PR Preview has run.\r\n\r\nIf you think your PR is ready to land, please double-check that the build is passing and the checklist is complete before pinging.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   * Chromium\r\n   * WebKit (as per @annevk)\r\n   * Mozilla (as per @mozfreddyb)\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62492\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chromium: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/562116090\r\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2062652 , https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2081266\r\n   * WebKit: doesn't require its own bug report\r\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46132\r\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\r\n\r\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12756/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 13, 2026, 5:33 PM UTC (b89833e)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12756/98753fa...b89833e/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 13, 2026, 5:33 PM UTC (b89833e)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12756/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 13, 2026, 5:33 PM UTC (b89833e)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12756/98753fa...b89833e/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 13, 2026, 5:33 PM UTC (b89833e)\">diff</a> )",
